## 2. Per-sample production plan (generated; PENDING = not yet known, never invented)
@@PLAN@@

Notes. **N sizing (VERIFY #6):** N_required uses σ_N = max(primary σ, PY8 test σ) × 1.05 (so the N rule cannot fail after production for a ±2 % closure, 03 §7b); the D-WH-3 top-up σ are the samples' own test values (ggZH 74.94 fb, ZH table 74.33; ttH dilepton 18.26, ZH table 18.11; ZH→ττ PY8 25.35 after matching, ZH table 24.97) and the larger is used. Fake-weighted pilots use the SR b-veto for both F_Wjjjj and T_ttjj_1l (b-veto has little effect on W+light jets: PEAK N_eff 18.5 vs 21.2 without). σ = LO MG5 (gridpack init σ preferred; smoke σ or frozen ZH σ otherwise, as stated per row). "N_planned" = accepted (Delphes-level) events; "[LHE gen.]" divides by the MLM/accept fraction of the test job. "Projected N_eff in SR" = test-job selected events in the **SR proxy** of `scripts/srsel.py` (not the final Phase 05 baseline) scaled to N_planned (unit weights ⇒ N_eff = N_sel); for 1-fake samples (ng = 1) it ignores the weight of the second (fake) photon, so it is an upper projection of the raw MC support. With 2000-event tests a low count carries a large Poisson error. CPU/storage use the per-sample test cost (s/event, kB/event) where a test exists, defaults 0.13 s/ev and 2.8 kB/ev otherwise.

**Rows waiting on the two long gridpacks (exactly):** `B_EW_Waajj_nomjj` (gridpack 884934.13: σ, N, cost, test job, and its EW twin production; follow-up `scripts/followup_after_gridpacks.sh test` then `... twinB`), `V_ZZa_WH` (gridpack 885044: σ, N, test job; follow-up `scripts/followup_after_gridpacks.sh test`). All other rows have a gridpack and a verified-by-executor test job; no other row is pending except where the table says PENDING for the verifier. Phase 03 PASS also needs these two test jobs.

