## 5. Seeds, duplicate check and condor submission plan
Seeds: formula and J-ranges in §1; G2-prep seeds `config/seeds_g2.txt` (57 incl. EW twins), production seeds `scripts/make_prod_sub.py` (uniqueness asserted). **Submitted so far (pre-G2 allowed):** gridpacks cluster **884934** (16 procs, one per new sample), test jobs cluster **884935** (21 procs, hold-and-release until the gridpack exists), QCD twin jobs cluster **884936** (10 procs: 5 × 8000 ev for each of B_QCD_Waajj_nomjj, F_QCD_Wajj_nomjj, LHE kept), earlier clusters 884456 (gridpacks, 884456.3 running), 884457 (tests), 884460, 884860. `condor_q` was checked before each submission (no existing job of the same name). The EW twin production jobs (`work/condor/g2_twins_ew.sub`, 2 × 5 × 8000 ev) are prepared and will be submitted after their EW test jobs succeed. **After G2:** one cluster per sample from `work/condor/prod/prod_<sample>.sub` (generated for every sample with known N; the rest after their σ is known), each preceded by a `condor_q` duplicate check, stage-out to `p2/production/wh/<sample>/`, the wrapper skips existing outputs and never overwrites (no duplicates by construction).

## 6. tt̄γ / tWγ vs tt̄γγ overlap after the b-veto (G1 item 4)
@@TTG@@
Reading: zero MC events pass the SR proxy in the 2000-event tests. **Zero is not a bound.** The 95 % CL upper limits on the removed (≥2-prompt-photon) yield after the b-veto and SR-proxy selection, at 500 fb⁻¹, are **< 373 events (T_tta_1l), < 57 events (T_tWa_1l)**, and < 0.42 events for the full T_ttaa_1l (3-event Poisson limits ×σ·k·L/N); they are uninformative and the overlap is **not** declared negligible. Measured: the ≥2-prompt-photon fraction is 1.3 % (T_tta_1l) and 1.45 % (T_tWa_1l); the removed part has σ·k ≈ 6.5 fb and 1.1 fb before selection versus 0.564 fb for T_ttaa_1l. The removal is applied (as in ZH). **How to get a usable bound:** a limit below 1 event needs N > 3·σ·k·L = 7.5×10⁵ (T_tta_1l) and 1.1×10⁵ (T_tWa_1l) events; the planned production samples (T_tta_1l 1.57×10⁶, T_tWa_1l 2.3×10⁵) reach this, so the bound is computed from the ≥2-prompt-photon subset of those samples in Phase 05 (no extra generation), with the T_ttaa_1l yield as the comparison; if it is not small, a 100 % systematic on the T_tta_1l 2-photon component is carried.

## 6b. QCD-type PS/merging uncertainty (G2 item 7), declared before Phase 06
The 40k twins show that for 14-45 % of reco-SR events (m_jj>500) the parton pair from the 2-jet ME has m_jj below 100-400 GeV: the tag jets then come from the parton shower (or from fake-photon jets), where fixed-order LO 2-jet B_QCD/F_QCD samples are not NLL-accurate. Declared: **100 % uncertainty on the PS-jet fraction of the QCD-type samples** (B_QCD_Waajj_nomjj, F_QCD_Wajj_nomjj, ZH_Zaajj_QCD_nomjj_lostlep, QCD part of ZH_Zajj_eFake, Q_aajj, T_tta/T_tWa), i.e. an uncertainty of ±(0.15…0.45 [twin loss fractions at 100…400 GeV]) × yield, nominal ±45 %·yield, correlated across QCD-type samples; to be replaced if an MLM Wγ(γ)+2,3j cross-check (not generated) shows smaller differences. The ME-jet W+4j/tt̄jj samples (F_Wjjjj, T_ttjj_1l) do not carry it. Also declared: LO αs⁴ scale envelope for F_Wjjjj/T_ttjj_1l (7-point), and the 2-fake f-scenarios ×{0.09, 1, 9} (review item 12).

## 6c. Lost-lepton coverage bound (G2 item 5)
Generator lepton cuts bound the covered phase space: `ZH_Zajj_eFake` (ptl>10, |η|<2.5, mmll>50) and `V_*_WH` (ptl>5, |η|<3.5, mmll>10). Bound by σ ratios: (i) `F_QCD_llajj_loose` (ZH card, mmjj 0, loose lepton cuts; gridpack 885124) vs the ZH-cut σ = 817.8 fb: the ratio σ_loose/σ_tight − 1 is carried as a one-sided systematic on the lost-lepton part of `ZH_Zajj_eFake` (PENDING the gridpack σ); (ii) V_WZa_WH loose σ (gridpack, cuts above) vs the ZH `V_WZa` σ = 2.203 fb (tight cuts) gives the same ratio for the V samples (value in §2 once σ known). Phase space beyond |η|<3.5 / pT<5 is not covered and is stated as such.

## 6d. N_eff rule enforcement and top-up rule (G2 item 4)
`scripts/make_plan.py` runs a **self-test that writes nothing** (a bad row must make `neff_gate` and `br_ledger.nmc_check` fail; 3/3 failures-as-expected are printed in `work/plan_nmc.txt`), populates the BR ledger from the matrix (so `nmc_check` cannot be a no-op; it refuses to PASS with zero rows or rows without a ledger entry), plans N from a design target N_eff = 30, and then applies `neff_gate` to the **final emitted N_planned** using the measured pilot N_eff per event. It exits non-zero if any weighted/fake-model row has projected N_eff < 10 in the PEAK (final-SR-like) region of its pilot or no PEAK event at all (use a larger test), or N_planned > 2×10⁷. Projections use photons **pT>25** (the SR value; the earlier 185/293 used pT>20): F_Wjjjj 163, T_ttjj_1l 258, F_QCD_Wajj_nomjj 8.7×10³, F_EW_Wajj_nomjj 391, T_tta_1l 1.6×10³, T_tWa_1l 360 (see §2). **Top-up rule:** after production, the Phase 05 SR N_eff (Σw)²/Σw² of each weighted row is recomputed with the final baseline; if < 10, the row is topped up with new jobs (seeds J ≥ 500, same card and gridpack) to N_topup = N_planned × (12/N_eff,SR − 1); if the top-up would exceed 2×10⁷ events, the 95 % upper limit of that component is carried as a conservative variant (D-WH policy, as HH §4.3). Indicative test-job yields (500 fb⁻¹, f0 = 10⁻³, N_eff mostly 1-30, large statistical errors): F_QCD_Wajj_nomjj PEAK 3.0 events (N_eff 1.0), F_EW_Wajj_nomjj 0.15 (1.5), T_tta_1l 0.20 (2.0), T_tWa_1l 0.04 (3.0), F_Wjjjj 1.15 (16), T_ttjj_1l 0.32 (26) versus signal ≈ 0.9; the 1-fake Wγjj component is thus comparable to the signal.

## 6e. Non-prompt-lepton class (G2 item 1)
Samples with no real lepton: `Q_aajj` (QCD γγ+jj, σ_smoke 3.54 pb with pta>25, 100<mγγ<170), `H_VBFH_jj` (VBF H→γγ+jj, gridpack σ = 4.124 pb, includes hadronic VH at EW order 3), `H_ggF_jj` (ggF-like H+jj via the top loop, LO loop-induced; no K-factor). Per-jet probability weights (`scripts/fakelep_pilot.py`): each reco jet with pT>25, |η|<2.5 may be the lepton (x·pT>25, x~N(0.85,0.1)) with weight f_ℓ; SR-like selection: no real lepton, MET>30 (event MET, **assumption**), two photons pT>25, 120<mγγ<130, two tag jets (m_jj>500, |Δη|>2.5), b-veto. **f_ℓ is PENDING D28**: yields are reported at both ends of the assumed range (3×10⁻⁵ and 10⁻³; nominal 10⁻⁴, an assumption anchored to nothing published until D28 is answered); N_eff does not depend on f_ℓ. **Test-job results (5000 events each, 500 fb⁻¹, PEAK region; yields at f_ℓ = 3×10⁻⁵ / 10⁻⁴ / 10⁻³):** `Q_aajj` (885126.0, gridpack σ 3.58 pb) 3 raw events, N_eff 2.8: **0.054 / 0.18 / 1.8 events**; `H_VBFH_jj` (885125.0) 77 raw events, N_eff 58: **0.0031 / 0.0105 / 0.105 events**; `H_ggF_jj` PENDING (loop gridpack 885122.2 still running; if it fails, D-WH-14). Both are the same order as the earlier assumed-ε estimates (QCD γγ+jj 0.07/0.25/2.5; VBF 0.0038/0.0127/0.127), which is now MC-supported for the pilot selection, but the QCD γγ+jj value is not negligible against the signal ≈ 0.9 events at the high end and rests on 3 raw events (N_eff 2.8): the planned N (§2) is sized for N_eff ≥ 10. The earlier ESTIMATE (0.07/0.25/2.5 events for QCD γγ+jj, ε assumed) remains labelled an estimate; the tt̄ case (estimate 0.010 vs MC 0.32 events) shows why.

